  "# ADR-2607198300: kotoba must own AOT compilation to a standalone artifact — no JVM/Node/Rust bypass; kotoba-lang/compiler already has a working native x86_64/aarch64 codegen backend

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Context

ADR-2607198200 (same day, same session) proved the compile -> `kotoba wasm emit`
-> execute loop works for a Stripe Customer create/get/list actor, first via
JVM/Chicory then via Node-native WebAssembly against
`kotoba-lang/wasm-webcomponent`'s browser-native `kgraph.js`. The owner then
asked to raise kotoba's own AOT-compilation maturity so execution needs no
JVM, no Node, no browser JS engine, and no new Rust or C runtime — kotoba's
own compiler must own the whole path from source to a directly-runnable,
standalone artifact ('kotoba が AOT compile を最後まで面倒を見る').

## What was ruled out, and why

- **JVM** (`kototama.tender` / `kotoba.wasm-exec` via com.dylibso.chicory) —
  owner-flagged deprecated for this purpose.
- **A JS engine** (Node or a real browser tab running
  `wasm-webcomponent`'s `kgraph.js`/`actor-host.js`) — this is
  `kototama`'s own R2, and `kototama`'s own `docs/maturity.md` ladder
  (R0 contract → **R1 JVM/Chicory, stable** → **R2 browser-native, advanced-partial**
  → R3 fleet-on-R1) confirms directly (not inferred) that there is no tier
  beyond R1/R2 today — R2 is browser-*native*, not machine-native.
- **`clojurewasm`** — still import-free-module-only FFI as of 2026-07-19; no
  newer notes anywhere in this workspace suggest upstream's promised fuller
  host-import FFI ('Phase-16') has landed. Out of this org's control.
- **A new Rust-embedded execution engine** (e.g. wasmtime-via-Rust) — directly
  contradicts the already-accepted org-wide policy in
  `90-docs/adr/2607072000-kotoba-rust-avoidance-policy-and-kotoba-server-gap.edn`
  ('anything that would need Rust: implement in cljc instead'), grounded in
  this org's own history of deleting kotoba-lang/kotoba's ~380k-line Rust
  crate tree (former kotoba-server engine, PR #259) in favor of the current
  thin CLJ launcher.

## Precedent for the one narrow exception

`kotoba-lang/aiueos`'s own README states it 'no longer owns a Rust runtime
crate' (JVM/Chicory covers its hosted Wasm execution), while its
`os/aiueos` bare-metal profile (16 `.c` + 4 `.S` files) owns the native
bootloader/kernel implementation. This org already treats **C as acceptable
only at the true OS-executable-format boundary** (an entry-point/crt0-equivalent
shim) — never as a general execution engine or a Rust substitute.

## Discovery: kotoba-lang/compiler already has almost exactly what was asked for

`kotoba-lang/compiler` — a separate git dependency from `kotoba-lang/kotoba`,
containing the canonical `guest-grammar.edn` and a stricter compile backend —
already implements:

- `src/kotoba/compiler/backend/x86_64.clj` (289 lines) and
  `backend/aarch64.clj` (186 lines): hand-written native machine-code
  generators in **pure cljc** — direct raw x86-64/AArch64 opcode emission,
  SysV/AAPCS64 calling convention, fuel/gas metering, tail-self-call
  optimization, and a working `pair`/heap-arena construct. No LLVM, no Rust,
  no wasmtime anywhere in this codegen path.
- `test/kotoba/compiler/native_executor_test.clj`: proves genuine, real
  native execution end to end —
  `verified-native-execution-produces-measured-evidence` (real result `42`),
  `native-trap-is-returned-as-measured-evidence` (real OS
  signal/trap detection), `bounded-pair-arena-executes-and-rejects-forged-handles`
  (real heap-arena semantics) — via `ProcessBuilder`-invoked, then
  natively-OS-executed binaries. Once the artifact exists, no JVM/Node/browser
  is present at all.
- The **only** non-cljc code in this entire pipeline is
  `tools/kexe_loader.c` (+ `_windows.c`): a minimal, SHA256-pinned,
  'reviewed POSIX native loader source' (`runtime_identity.clj`) — a
  crt0-equivalent OS entry-point stub compiled by the system's own `cc`/`clang`.
  Not a runtime, not a Rust substitute — the same narrow exception aiueos
  already established.
- `target.clj` additionally declares (as target-profile *data*, not yet
  all implemented) `:x86_64-aiueos-kernel-v1`/`:x86_64-aiueos-user-v1`
  profiles with `:runtime :none` and `:host-imports false` — genuinely
  runtime-free freestanding artifacts for the aiueos bare-metal context.

`kotoba-lang/kotobase` was also checked and found irrelevant to this
question: it is a Datomic-analog datom database built *on* the kotoba
language's `[e a v]` model, with no WASM-hosting concern of its own.

## Gap and next step

This native backend does not yet support `kgraph-assert!`/`kgraph-query`
(the EAVT datom-store capability ADR-2607198200's Customer pilot exercised)
— only pure computation plus the `pair`/heap-arena construct, the same
limited op-surface as this same repo's own `backend/wasm.cljc` (190 lines,
hardcodes exactly `pair`/`pair-first`/`pair-second` under module
`'kotoba:heap'`; no generic host-import declaration/dispatch table exists
yet to extend).

**Next step (in progress as of this ADR's authoring):** port
`kgraph-assert!`/`kgraph-query` into `backend/aarch64.clj` (this development
machine is Apple Silicon/arm64) following the same pattern as the existing
`pair`-arena, then re-run the Customer create/get/list pilot
(ADR-2607198200) targeting `:aarch64-macos-kotoba-v1` to prove it genuinely
native end to end — no JVM, no Node, no browser, no new Rust, only the
existing reviewed C loader shim.

## Policy (durable, recorded here and in root CLAUDE.md)

For kotoba-lang: 'avoid JVM/Node/Rust at runtime' means **kotoba's own
compiler (cljc) must own AOT compilation all the way to a standalone,
directly-runnable native artifact** — the delivered EXECUTION must not
depend on a JVM/Chicory host, a JS engine (Node or browser) host, or a new
Rust execution engine. The compiler TOOLING itself may still run on the JVM
today (a build-time concern, like any compiler needing some host to run on
— not a runtime dependency of the produced artifact). The sole sanctioned
non-cljc component anywhere in this path is a minimal, reviewed,
hash-pinned OS entry-point loader shim (crt0-equivalent), exactly the
aiueos `os/` precedent — never a general-purpose C/Rust runtime or
execution engine standing in for kotoba's own codegen."}]
